WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.010
A line of French dialogue:

2
00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.980
«C'est injuste». And then just two words:

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.310
«dit-elle». Verb first, subject second.

4
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.730
Isn't that how French asks a question?

5
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.450
Then a sentence opens with «Peut-être»,

6
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.140
and the verb flips again:

7
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.610
«Peut-être a-t-il raison.» A mistake?

8
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.940
A hidden question?

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.450
Something else? Why do French
writers flip the verb like this?

10
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.680
In this mission, you'll watch verb
and subject chips swap places,

11
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.960
and see what slips in between them.

12
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.180
Then you'll flip sentences yourself,

13
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.080
starting with the mayor's reply:

14
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.430
«Je refuse». Your mission: find
out why the verb jumps the queue.
